issues.body:
`- name: Clippy (release feature union, -D warnings)` runs `cargo clippy --all-targets --features hdt,federation,odrl,forms,custom-protocol` inside the `tauri-build` job. That job's steps are checkout → apt (Linux) → rustup → cache → clippy/build/test only — there is no `actions/setup-node`, no `npm install`, no wasm build, and no `gui/app` `build:tauri`.

`custom-protocol` flips `cfg(dev)` to false (gui/src-tauri/Cargo.toml documents `let dev = !custom_protocol`). With `dev == false`, `tauri::generate_context!()` (gui/src-tauri/src/lib.rs:93) takes the asset-embedding branch, and tauri-codegen 2.6.3 `context.rs:186-190` does:

    FrontendDist::Directory(path) => {
      let assets_path = config_parent.join(path);
      if !assets_path.exists() {
        panic!("The `frontendDist` configuration is set to `{path:?}` but this path doesn't exist")
      }

`frontendDist` is `../app/out` (tauri.conf.json) and `gui/app/out` is gitignored (gui/app/.gitignore:3) — it exists only after `npm run build:tauri`. Every other `--features custom-protocol` build in this repo builds it first and says so explicitly (gui.yml:673-676 "the frontend MUST be built first"; gui.yml:687-699 and 822-831).

Consequence: the union lane is expected to fail on all five matrix rows with a proc-macro panic before it ever exercises feature unification. Because `tauri-build` is `continue-on-error: true` and `advisory` (gui.yml:441-458), it will not block anything — it will just be permanently red, which is exactly the kind of ignorable noise that hides a real unification break later. The existing non-custom-protocol lanes pass only because `dev == true` short-circuits the asset check.

The other new lanes (`hdt`, `forms`) are fine — this is specific to the `custom-protocol` member of the union.
